  "conclusion": "Route2 nested-L2 is the best AMR accuracy (Cd=1.1573, 6.00%, 45% memory saving), approaching uniform-R16 (4.45%). Route1 body-fitted shell gives 86.3% memory saving at 7.97% (\u2248 single-block 7.80%). Route3 cellwise adaptive failed on GPU (sphere cover 90.8%, Cd error >600%) \u2014 coarse-grid patch BFL weighting unreliable. Combo shell+L2 saves 97.9% memory but error degrades to 18.8%: the shell removes the thick fine region around the whole sphere that carries the boundary-layer/pressure development \u2014 blunt-body flows need that volume, shell-only refinement suits slender bodies (SUBOFF) instead."
}